# What EAS Build uploads.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: build 26 died in "Install dependencies" after 44 seconds.
# `apps/desktop-agent/` is UNTRACKED and NOT gitignored, so it rode along in the
# archive — and it has a package.json that is not in pnpm-lock.yaml, so
# `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` failed on EAS with ERR_PNPM_OUTDATED_LOCKFILE
# exactly as it does locally. EAS archives untracked files too; "it isn't
# committed" is NOT the same as "EAS won't see it".
#
# 🔴 THIS FILE REPLACES .gitignore FOR EAS — INCLUDING EVERY NESTED ONE.
# The moment it exists, apps/mobile/.gitignore stops being consulted, so its
# `/ios` rule no longer applies and a local prebuild (1.1 GB here) would upload.
# Every rule below that mirrors a .gitignore is load-bearing; deleting one does
# not "fall back" to git's copy.
#
# WHAT MUST STAY: every pnpm workspace member's package.json (apps/mobile,
# apps/web, packages/db, packages/shared). Excluding one makes a frozen-lockfile
# install fail on a missing importer — the same class of failure this file fixes.
# apps/desktop-agent is the one exception: it matches the apps/* glob but is
# absent from the lockfile, which is precisely why it has to go.

# ── Dependencies (mirrors root .gitignore; both forms on purpose — a SYMLINK
#    named node_modules slips past the directory-only form) ────────────────────
node_modules/
node_modules
.pnpm-store/

# ── Build / cache ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.next/
.turbo/
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo
.playwright-mcp/
.superpowers/

# ── Expo / React Native ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.expo/
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
*.orig.*

# Generated native projects — from apps/mobile/.gitignore, restated with full
# paths. NOT a bare `ios/`: apps/mobile/modules/nemesis-audio-encoder/ios is a
# real source directory the build needs.
apps/mobile/ios/
apps/mobile/android/
apps/mobile/web-build/
apps/mobile/expo-env.d.ts
apps/mobile/.metro-health-check*
apps/mobile/deno.lock
apps/mobile/test-results/
apps/mobile/playwright-report/
apps/mobile/.playwright/
apps/mobile/e2e/.auth/

# ── Env / secrets. EAS injects the build profile's own env, so a local .env
#    must never be uploaded. ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Supabase ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/

# ── OS / editor ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
*.log
.idea/
.vscode/
.vercel
.hermes-ref/
graphify-out/

# ── THE ACTUAL FIX: a workspace-glob member with no lockfile entry ────────────
apps/desktop-agent/

# ── Untracked weight the phone build has no use for. The archive was 455 MB;
#    the git tree alone is 127 MB, so most of it was images and scratch. ───────
marketing/
tmp/
apps/nemesis-desktop/
landing/
.obsidian/
.gstack/
.claude/worktrees/

# Loose screenshots and scratch notes dumped at the REPO ROOT. Every pattern is
# anchored with a leading slash so it matches only the root. A bare `*.png`
# would also swallow apps/mobile/assets/images/icon.png and splash-icon.png —
# both required build inputs and fingerprint sources — and re-including them
# with a `!` negation is a footgun that fails silently at 44 seconds.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.canvas
/Untitled*
